  "Number": 25,
  "Question": "The symbol \\(|a|\\) means \\(+a\\) if \\(a\\) is greater than or equal to zero, and \\(-a\\) if \\(a\\) is less than or equal to zero; the symbol \\(\\lt\\) means “less than”; the symbol \\(\\gt\\) means “greater than.” The set of values \\(x\\) satisfying the inequality \\(|3-x|\\lt4\\) consists of all \\(x\\) such that:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(x^2\\lt49\\)",
    "B": "\\(x^2\\gt1\\)",
    "C": "\\(1\\lt x^2\\lt49\\)",
    "D": "\\(-1\\lt x\\lt7\\)",
    "E": "\\(-7\\lt x\\lt1\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Absolute value measures distance, so \\(|3-x|=|x-3|\\) is the distance between \\(x\\) and \\(3\\) on the number line. A distance less than \\(4\\) places \\(x\\) strictly between the points \\(4\\) units to either side of \\(3\\):\n\\[\n3-4<x<3+4.\n\\]\nThus \\(-1<x<7\\). Both endpoints are excluded because each gives \\(|3-x|=4\\), while every point between them has distance less than \\(4\\). The answer is choice D.",
